#   BUG-EXTRACT-STRING-NEG1-CONTINUES [_extract_string — when _get_length_fast returns
#             -1 (oracle dead) AND the slow _get_length also returns -1, the function
#             falls through to char-by-char extraction instead of returning "" immediately]:
#             ROOT CAUSE: _extract_string() checks:
#               if _length == 0: retry slow; if still 0: return ""
#               if _length > 0:  set max_len = _length
#               else:            log "length unknown, max N"  ← catches -1
#             When _get_length_fast returns -1 (oracle failure) the `if _length == 0:`
#             branch is skipped (−1 ≠ 0).  The `if _length > 0:` branch is also skipped
#             (−1 is not > 0).  The `else:` branch logs "length unknown" and extraction
#             continues using max_len as the upper bound.  Every subsequent _eval() call
#             also returns None (oracle is still dead), so the consecutive-fail counter
