#   BUG-SCHEMA-ENUMERATOR-COCKROACHDB-FALLBACK [SchemaEnumeratorV18.__init__ —
#             CockroachDB (also YugabyteDB and DuckDB) falls back to MySQL GROUP_CONCAT
#             queries instead of PostgreSQL string_agg, breaking ALL SchemaEnumeratorV18
#             extractions on CockroachDB targets]:
#             ROOT CAUSE: SchemaEnumeratorV18.__init__ initialised self._queries with:
#               self._queries = self.QUERIES.get(dbms, self.QUERIES.get("MySQL", {}))
#             QUERIES is a class-level dict with explicit entries for MySQL, MariaDB,
#             MSSQL, PostgreSQL, Oracle, SQLite, DB2, Firebird, SAP_HANA, and ClickHouse —
#             but NO entry for "CockroachDB", "YugabyteDB", or "DuckDB".  For these
#             DBMSes, self.QUERIES.get(dbms) returned None and the fallback
#             self.QUERIES.get("MySQL", {}) was used — setting self._queries to the MySQL
#             QUERIES dict, which uses GROUP_CONCAT(... SEPARATOR ',') syntax.
#             CockroachDB does NOT support GROUP_CONCAT with SEPARATOR; it supports
#             string_agg (PostgreSQL-compatible syntax).  _get_query() contains a
#             parent_map that routes CockroachDB → PostgreSQL, but this map fires ONLY
#             when self._queries.get(key, "") returns an empty string.  Since MySQL has
#             non-empty entries for every key ("dbs", "tables", "columns", "row_chunked",
#             etc.), the parent_map condition `if not q:` was NEVER True for CockroachDB.
#             Consequence: every call to get_dbs(), get_tables(), get_columns(), and
#             dump_rows() for CockroachDB sent MySQL GROUP_CONCAT syntax, which
#             CockroachDB rejects — silently producing empty results for ALL schema
#             enumeration and data extraction on CockroachDB targets via this engine.
#             YugabyteDB and DuckDB were affected by the same root cause (both are
#             PostgreSQL-wire-compatible and have no explicit QUERIES entry).
#             Fix: resolve the parent_map at __init__ time — before any _get_query()
#             call — so self._queries is initialised to the correct parent DBMS dict:
#               CockroachDB / YugabyteDB / DuckDB → PostgreSQL QUERIES
#               MariaDB / TiDB                    → MySQL QUERIES
#             DBMSes not in QUERIES and not in the parent_map still fall back to MySQL
#             as the least-bad default.  The _get_query() parent_map is kept as a second-
#             level fallback for keys absent even in the parent dict (e.g. fallback-only
#             keys that exist in PostgreSQL but not in the primary QUERIES for that DBMS).
