#             to `else: return []`, making all error-based column enumeration on
#             CockroachDB silently return an empty column list]:
#             ROOT CAUSE: Same missing-branch pattern as BUG-COCKROACHDB-ERROR-TABLES.
#             The column enumeration dispatch also had no CockroachDB case, causing
#             every column enumeration attempt on CockroachDB to log "Unsupported DBMS"
#             and return [].  With no column list, _error_dump_table was never called
#             and extraction stopped silently after the table enumeration phase.
#             Fix: merge CockroachDB into the PostgreSQL elif branch.
#
#   BUG-PG-ERROR-COLS-PUBLIC-SCHEMA [_error_enum_columns — PostgreSQL/CockroachDB
#             col_query_tpl and count_query hardcode table_schema='public',
#             returning 0 columns for tables in non-public schemas]:
#             ROOT CAUSE: Same root cause as BUG-PG-ERROR-TABLES-PUBLIC-SCHEMA.
