        # database contains a genuine NUL byte (chr(0)) — return chr(0) so callers can
        # include it in extracted strings. When lo==0 after an EARLY EXIT, the search
        # never confirmed anything — return None to signal extraction failure so the
        # caller retries or marks the position as unknown.
