                # "SUBSTRING-num+size(548vs146)" (size delta, numeric-ctx) split at "(" to give
                # "SUBSTRING" vs "SUBSTRING-num+size" — treated as DIFFERENT families despite
                # testing the SAME SQL function SUBSTRING. A dynamic page returning different-
                # sized error pages for any malformed SQL satisfies both, producing a false-positive
                # confirmation. Fix: normalize family names to strip context suffixes ("-num",
                # "-DUAL", "-str") and "+size" so same-function different-context pairs are grouped
                # correctly. "SUBSTRING" and "LENGTH" remain different families (correct).
                # BUG-INLINE-RE-IMPORT-FIX: use module-level _re
                # BUG-V28-2 FIX (Req 9/CPU): _norm_chka_family was defined INSIDE this loop body,
                # causing Python to allocate a new function object on every iteration.  Moved out
